sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Small changes in the relative sizes of the four cells carry the median partition and its polar furrows through all their possible arrangements, which correspond to those observed in various embryos; these arrangements are physical phenomena distributed without relation to zoological classification, not species characters.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Polar-furrow arrangements follow relative cell sizes, not species identity";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter VII, “The Forms of Tissues, or Cell-Aggregates”; topic “Polar furrow variants and cell size”. Scope: four-celled stage of embryos across molluscs, annelids, coelenterates, vertebrates and others"
}
